The rationale for including a "SimplifyEquation" task before the "FindRoots" task can be questioned because finding the roots of an equation inherently involves simplifying it. However, breaking down the process into distinct tasks ensures clarity and modularity in the workflow.

Combining these tasks could streamline the process by reducing redundancy. Instead of explicitly stating a separate "SimplifyEquation" step, you can integrate this within the "FindRoots" task. This approach maintains the logical flow while minimizing unnecessary steps.

Here’s an updated version of your TG:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "GeoTrigo",
    "tasks": {
        "ExpandPolynomials": "Expanding the polynomials on both sides of the equation",
        "FindRoots": "Finding the roots of the simplified polynomial equation (including simplification)"
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "ExpandPolynomials",
            "to": "FindRoots"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

This revised TG removes the redundant "SimplifyEquation" task and combines its functionality with the "FindRoots" task, ensuring all necessary steps are covered while maintaining a clear and concise workflow.
